
Lab 08 for the Machine Learning Lab course, focusing on building, optimizing, and evaluating deep learning models 
for computer vision tasks. The workflow involves developing a custom Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) architecture 
using Keras/TensorFlow, integrating sequential convolutional filtering, batch normalization, max-pooling, and dropout
regularization layers to perform binary and multi-class classification on plant disease imagery, and thoroughly auditing
the resulting model's classification dynamics using comprehensive evaluation matrices such as classification reports, precision,
recall, and accuracy tracking scores.
